tsApp template metadata from Meta and template parameters with Liquid variables. Use `GET /v1/environments/{environment_id}/whatsapp/templates` to list templates.\",\"example\":\"{\\\"body\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"image_url\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"whatsapp_message_template\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"12345\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"welcome\\\",\\\"language\\\":\\\"en_US\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"APPROVED\\\",\\\"components\\\":[...]},\\\"template_parameters\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"welcome\\\",\\\"components\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"BODY\\\",\\\"parameters\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"{{customer.name}}\\\",\\\"parameter_name\\\":\\\"name\\\"}]}]}}\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"body_json\":{\"description\":\"For visual editor content (if applicable).\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"broadcast_id\":{\"description\":\"The identifier for a broadcast.\",\"example\":2,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"created\":{\"description\":\"The date time when the referenced ID was created.\",\"example\":1552341937,\"format\":\"unix timestamp\",\"readOnly\":true,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"deduplicate_id\":{\"description\":\"An identifier in the format `id:timestamp` where the id is for the object you're working with (Automations, Deliveries, Exports, Identities, One-time sends, Segments, and Templates), and the timestamp is the last time the object was updated.\",\"example\":\"15:1492548073\",\"readOnly\":true,\"type\":\"string\"},\"id\":{\"description\":\"The identifier for an action.\",\"example\":96,\"readOnly\":true,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"language\":{\"description\":\"The language variant for your message. If you don't use our [localization feature](/journeys/channels/localization/getting-started), or this is the default message, this value is an empty string.\",\"example\":\"fr\",\"readOnly\":true,\"type\":\"string\"},\"name\":{\"description\":\"The name of the action.\",\"example\":\"Welcome Message\",\"readOnly\":true,\"type\":\"string\"},\"recipient\":{\"description\":\"The recipient's phone number in E.164 format, usually referenced with Liquid like `{{customer.phone}}`. If you use Liquid, this field is blank in `GET` responses because we resolve the recipient at send time.\",\"example\":\"\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"send_to_unsubscribed\":{\"description\":\"Whether to send this message to unsubscribed customers.\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"sender_identity_id\":{\"description\":\"The ID of the WhatsApp Business phone number to send from. This corresponds to\\na phone number registered in your WhatsApp Business Account and synced via\\n`GET /v1/environments/{environment_id}/whatsapp/sync`.\\n\",\"type\":\"integer\"},\"sending_state\":{\"description\":\"Determines the sending behavior for the action. `automatic` sends the action automatically when triggered; `draft` queues drafts when the action is triggered; or `off` to disable the action.\",\"enum\":[\"automatic\",\"draft\",\"off\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"tracked\":{\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Whether links in template parameters should be tracked.\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"type\":{\"description\":\"For WhatsApp messages sent from Customer.io using your Facebook Business Account (not Twilio), the `type` is always `whatsapp`.\",\"enum\":[\"whatsapp\"],\"readOnly\":true,\"type\":\"string\"},\"updated\":{\"description\":\"The date time when the referenced ID was last updated.\",\"example\":1552341937,\"format\":\"unix timestamp\",\"readOnly\":true,\"type\":\"integer\"}},\"title\":\"WhatsApp\"},{\"properties\":{\"body\":{\"description\":\"The body of the action. You cannot modify the body if you created it with our drag-and-drop editor.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"broadcast_id\":{\"description\":\"The identifier for a broadcast.\",\"example\":2,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"created\":{\"description\":\"The date time when the referenced ID was created.\",\"example\":1552341937,\"format\":\"unix timestamp\",\"readOnly\":true,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"deduplicate_id\":{\"description\":\"An identifier in the format `id:timestamp` where the 